MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "A Pentatonix Christmas feels like a natural next choice because it combines Christmas songs and vocal harmonies, connecting my holiday listening with my interest in The New Old Fashioned.",
    "Orla Fallon's Celtic Christmas connects with my repeated interest in Christmas albums, while Carpenters Gold and Michael Bublé appeal to my interest in gentle vocal music, though I am less ready to choose those."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Bread, Lesley Gore and Willie Nelson collections do not give me the Christmas and vocal-harmony connection that makes Pentatonix appealing right now.",
    "A Musical Affair, Stages and The Ultimate Collection give me too little information about the music to feel confident that they match my interests; I would usually pass unless the connection were clearer."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that an interest in gentle vocal music extends to a broad range of older pop and artist retrospectives.",
    "A Christmas theme gets my attention, but it does not make every Christmas album equally appealing; I would still want to hear whether the musical style suits me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of Christmas songs and vocal harmonies matters more to me than either a holiday title or a broadly similar vocal style alone.",
    "There is a difference between music I might enjoy and music I would choose now: Pentatonix gives me a clear connection, while Bublé and Celtic Christmas would need a track check or a sample."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in Christmas and vocal music, but stretched that interest too broadly into collections I have little reason to choose now."
}
